  "term": "essentialism",
  "definition": "Essentialism, in this context, is the view that a primary caregiver’s role or suitability in infant care is determined by an inherent sexual belongingness. The source discusses rejecting this fixed, inborn account in favor of greater openness about sex and gender.",
